      "content": "The concept of absolute, 100% security is unattainable in any large-scale process, but that doesn't equate to operational compromise. Proponents counter that the risk of mass, successful manipulation through mail-in systems is significantly lower than the risks presented by other forms of election interference. The debate often centers on whether the incremental risks are acceptable compared to the benefits of accessibility these systems provide.",
